{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":20,"entries":[{"id":18030,"title":"Isaiah 20:1","segments":["¶In the year that Tartan came unto Ashdod, (when Sargon the king of Assyria sent him,) and fought against Ashdod, and took it;"],"ref":"Isaiah 20:1","verse":1,"words":[{"text":"¶In the year","strong":"H8141"},{"text":" that Tartan","strong":"H8661"},{"text":" came","strong":"H935"},{"text":" unto Ashdod","strong":"H795"},{"text":", (when Sargon","strong":"H5623"},{"text":" the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" of Assyria","strong":"H804"},{"text":" sent","strong":"H7971"},{"text":" him,) and fought","strong":"H3898"},{"text":" against Ashdod","strong":"H795"},{"text":", and took","strong":"H3920"},{"text":" it;"}]},{"id":18031,"title":"Isaiah 20:2","segments":["At the same time spake the LORD by Isaiah the son of Amoz, saying, Go and loose the sackcloth from off thy loins, and put off thy shoe from thy foot. And he did so, walking naked and barefoot. {by: Heb. by the hand of}"],"ref":"Isaiah 20:2","verse":2,"words":[{"text":"At the same time","strong":"H6256"},{"text":" spake","strong":"H1696"},{"text":" the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":" by","strong":"H3027"},{"text":" Isaiah","strong":"H3470"},{"text":" the son","strong":"H1121"},{"text":" of Amoz","strong":"H531"},{"text":", saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Go","strong":"H3212"},{"text":" and loose","strong":"H6605"},{"text":" the sackcloth","strong":"H8242"},{"text":" from off thy loins","strong":"H4975"},{"text":", and put off","strong":"H2502"},{"text":" thy shoe","strong":"H5275"},{"text":" from thy foot","strong":"H7272"},{"text":". And he did so","strong":"H6213"},{"text":", walking","strong":"H1980"},{"text":" naked","strong":"H6174"},{"text":" and barefoot","strong":"H3182"},{"text":". {by: Heb. by the hand of}"}]},{"id":18032,"title":"Isaiah 20:3","segments":["And the LORD said, Like as my servant Isaiah hath walked naked and barefoot three years [for] a sign and wonder upon Egypt and upon Ethiopia;"],"ref":"Isaiah 20:3","verse":3,"words":[{"text":"And the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":" said","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Like as my servant","strong":"H5650"},{"text":" Isaiah","strong":"H3470"},{"text":" hath walked","strong":"H1980"},{"text":" naked","strong":"H6174"},{"text":" and barefoot","strong":"H3182"},{"text":" three","strong":"H7969"},{"text":" years","strong":"H8141"},{"text":" [for] a sign","strong":"H226"},{"text":" and wonder","strong":"H4159"},{"text":" upon Egypt","strong":"H4714"},{"text":" and upon Ethiopia","strong":"H3568"},{"text":";"}]},{"id":18033,"title":"Isaiah 20:4","segments":["So shall the king of Assyria lead away the Egyptians prisoners, and the Ethiopians captives, young and old, naked and barefoot, even with [their] buttocks uncovered, to the shame of Egypt. {the Egyptians...: Heb. the captivity of Egypt} {shame: Heb. nakedness}"],"ref":"Isaiah 20:4","verse":4,"words":[{"text":"So shall the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" of Assyria","strong":"H804"},{"text":" lead away","strong":"H5090"},{"text":" the Egyptians","strong":"H4714"},{"text":" prisoners","strong":"H7628"},{"text":", and the Ethiopians","strong":"H3568"},{"text":" captives","strong":"H1546"},{"text":", young","strong":"H5288"},{"text":" and old","strong":"H2205"},{"text":", naked","strong":"H6174"},{"text":" and barefoot","strong":"H3182"},{"text":", even with [their] buttocks","strong":"H8357"},{"text":" uncovered","strong":"H2834"},{"text":", to the shame","strong":"H6172"},{"text":" of Egypt","strong":"H4714"},{"text":". {the Egyptians...: Heb. the captivity of Egypt} {shame: Heb. nakedness}"}]},{"id":18034,"title":"Isaiah 20:5","segments":["And they shall be afraid and ashamed of Ethiopia their expectation, and of Egypt their glory."],"ref":"Isaiah 20:5","verse":5,"words":[{"text":"And they shall be afraid","strong":"H2865"},{"text":" and ashamed","strong":"H954"},{"text":" of Ethiopia","strong":"H3568"},{"text":" their expectation","strong":"H4007"},{"text":", and of Egy